# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file for its "Cite this repository" button.
# Zenodo takes the metadata of each release from .zenodo.json; keep the two files in step.
# The DOI is the concept DOI of Zenodo, which resolves to the latest version.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "voxelFEM: a matrix-free GPU finite-element solver for elasticity on voxel grids"
abstract: >-
  voxelFEM is a finite-element solver for linear and nonlinear elasticity on voxel grids,
  written in Python with CuPy and run on one CUDA GPU. Every voxel is one trilinear
  hexahedral element, so a segmented CT scan or another 3-D image is simulated without
  meshing. The solver assembles no stiffness matrix and stores no element connectivity. It
  uses a Newton-Raphson iteration with load stepping, a preconditioned conjugate gradient
  method, and a Jacobi or a geometric multigrid preconditioner. Scripts map CT grey levels
  to a Young's modulus field, compute the effective modulus of a scan, and generate
  deformed images from the computed displacement field.
